  "id": "circular-reasoning",
  "term": "circular reasoning",
  "definition": "Circular reasoning is a faulty argument in which the conclusion, or a claim that depends on that conclusion, is used as part of the proof. It often appears as a chain of reasoning that loops back on itself instead of supplying independent support.",
